    <!--
      Romania is neither Ashkenaz nor Sefard. hamichlol notes that its readings
      follow the old Erets Yisrael rite, "לעומת מנהגי שאר העדות שמבוססים על המנהג
      הבבלי": as against the other rites, which follow the Babylonian custom.
      Parenting it to either would make its fallback claim the wrong tradition, so
      it hangs off Common and states its own readings.

      It says the same again of a particular reading: "ונראה שמנהג זה מבוסס על
      מסורה ארצישראלית, כמו רוב ההפטרות של רומניא": it appears this practice
      rests on an Erets Yisrael tradition, as do most of the Romania haftarot.
    -->
    <custom>
      <name n="Romania" lang="en" transliterated="true"/>
      <name n="Румыния (нусах романия)" lang="ru"/>
      <name n="רומניא" lang="he"/>
    </custom>
